Removes the fix of pieces-shorter-run-306.trace and pieces-shorter-run-414.trace:
`pieces` placing each line of a take from a source whose run holds it (in
tree_reconcile.rs). Without it, `pieces` merged every source's runs into one
list and looked only in the last run starting at or before a line, so a shorter
run of the same versions from a later source hid the head's whole run.
Base: the commit that adds this file; this hunk set is the reverse of its fix.
git: the release in ci/git-release.
Re-record (crates/agentfs-model/VERIFYING.md, "A regression found on the engine")
in a scratch worktree with this applied. Give it fresh volumes, since --record
refuses a non-empty OUT: export MODEL_TARGET_VOLUME=mt-fixture MODEL_WORK_VOLUME=mw-fixture
  for s in 306 414; do ci/model-docker.sh -- sh -c "AGENTFS_MODEL_TRACE_DIR=/work/t \
    AGENTFS_MODEL_SEED=$s cargo test --locked -p agentfs-model --test interleavings \
    random_interleavings_rounds_phase1_scope -- --exact"; done
  ci/model-docker.sh -- cargo run --locked -p agentfs-conformance --bin phase1-replay -- \
    library /work/t --min-scenarios 0 --min-seeds 1 --record /work/out
    # exits 1: MISMATCH at call 38 (seed 306) and call 127 (seed 414), as expected
  for s in 306 414; do ci/model-docker.sh -- sh -c "cp \
    /work/out/random_interleavings_rounds_phase1_scope.seed$s.trace \
    crates/agentfs-conformance/tests/regressions/pieces-shorter-run-$s.trace"; done
